From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: port: bind Offline/Host-command (O/H) ports (ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra, T-M6-8 rearch phase 1a)

Phase 1a of the OH-port-based VLAN re-architecture (see
plans/ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md), itself the proving ground for the same
OH-port re-enqueue primitive IPsec ESP offload needs (FE/CC ->
offline port -> CAAM QI -> SEC -> offline port re-parse -> TX FQ;
plans/OFFLOAD-CAPABILITY-PLAN.md S1.7, patch 0134-caam-qi-share
already lands the CAAM-side half of that hook).

mainline drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c has never
matched or probed Offline/Host-command (O/H) ports at all --
fman_port_match[] only lists fsl,fman-v3/v2-port-{rx,tx}. Confirmed
live on board .185 (image vyos-2026.09.01-0436-rolling) 2026-09-01:
/proc/device-tree/soc/fman@1a00000/ enumerates SIX
fsl,fman-v3-port-oh nodes (port@82000..port@87000, cell-index /
hw port id 0x02-0x07 -- more than arch/fman.md's "4 active O/H
ports 0x02-0x05" claimed; corrected there separately), none bound
to any driver. This patch makes them bindable.

Register layout (struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs) is transcribed
field-for-field from LS1046ADPAARM.pdf S5.5.4.7 "Offline Port/Host
Command Port Registers Description" (FMBM_OCFG at O/H port block
base FMan_base + 0x1000*n, n = hw port id, mirroring the existing
RX/TX port-page formula this project's board/scripts/pcd-snapshot
already relies on) -- offsets cross-checked against the RM's own
register-offset lines for every FMBM_O* register, not guessed.

Scope, deliberately narrow:
 - New FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH enum value (fman.h).
 - New struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs + union member (fman_port.c).
 - New "fsl,fman-v3-port-oh" of_device_id match + a probe() branch
   that only sets port_type/port_speed=0 -- IDENTICAL to the
   existing RX/TX branches in that no register is written; probe()
   as a whole never touches hardware, only maps the register window
   and stashes drvdata (see the existing function body, unchanged).
 - Extended the qman_channel_id lookup gate (previously TX-only) to
   also cover OH, since fman_get_qman_channel_id()'s port_ids[]
   table already carries 0x2/0x3/0x4/0x5/0x7 for O/H hw ids on this
   silicon rev (major<6) -- confirmed by reading fman.c, not by
   trial. Hw port 0x06 has no table entry and will simply fail this
   lookup and not register, which is fine (unused).
 - fman_port_lookup_oh(), mirroring the existing
   fman_port_lookup_rx() (patch 0115) active-port-registry pattern
   exactly, for a later increment to resolve the live struct
   fman_port once one exists.

Deliberately NOT in this patch: fman_port_config()/fman_port_init()
wiring for FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH (the RM 5.5.7.6 13-step FMBM_OCFG
bring-up: DMA attrs, internal-context params, dequeue/parser next-
engine, CC base, FQID, rate limiter, EN). No devicetree consumer
references any O/H node via fsl,fman-ports (only the six ethernet@
MAC nodes are referenced that way), so nothing calls config()/init()
on these new port objects -- this patch is provably inert as shipped:
it only makes six previously-invisible struct fman_port objects
enumerable, zero register writes, zero behavior change to any
existing RX/TX/CC/ehash/HMTD path. The bring-up sequence needs the
same register-exact care as this patch and touches the
resource-sizing helpers (get_dflt_num_of_{fifo_bufs,open_dmas,tasks})
shared with every RX/TX port on the chip -- a separate, board-gated
increment (phase 1b), not rushed into this one.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (new O/H port subsystem; probe-only, no register writes, no existing port type touched)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman.h      |   9 ++
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.h |   9 ++
 3 files changed, 128 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman.h
index c7b431705..0b8a68081 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman.h
@@ -83,6 +83,15 @@ struct fman; /* FMan data */
 enum fman_port_type {
 	FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX = 0,	/* TX Port */
 	FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX,	/* RX Port */
+	/*
+	 * Offline/Host-command (O/H) port -- RM 5.3.1 "FMan Hardware Ports
+	 * Types". No MAC; dequeues re-circulated frames from QMan, walks
+	 * Parser/KeyGen/CC via its own FMBM_O* BMI register block, then
+	 * re-enqueues. ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1); see
+	 * plans/ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md and the board-patch series near
+	 * 0175-fman-port-oh-type.patch for the bring-up this unlocks.
+	 */
+	FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH,
 };

 struct fman_rev_info {
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 01482f639..95ef9982b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -273,10 +273,71 @@ struct fman_port_tx_bmi_regs {
 	u32 reserved0310[0x3a]; /* (0x310-0x3FF) */
 };

+/*
+ * BMI Offline/Host-command (O/H) port register map -- RM 5.5.4.7, register
+ * offsets confirmed against LS1046ADPAARM.pdf (each O/H port's block lives
+ * at FMan_base + 0x1000*n, n = hw O/H port id; ASK2 dpaa1 board uses n=0x04,
+ * live-confirmed unbound 2026-09-01, see plans/ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md). Field
+ * order/offsets match the RM table exactly -- do not reorder.
+ */
+struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs {
+	u32 fmbm_ocfg;		/* O/H Configuration */
+	u32 fmbm_ost;		/* O/H Status */
+	u32 fmbm_oda;		/* O/H DMA attributes */
+	u32 fmbm_oicp;		/* O/H Internal Context Parameters */
+	u32 fmbm_ofdne;		/* O/H Frame Dequeue Next Engine */
+	u32 fmbm_ofne;		/* O/H Frame Next Engine */
+	u32 fmbm_ofca;		/* O/H Frame Command Attributes */
+	u32 fmbm_ofpne;		/* O/H Frame Parser Next Engine */
+	u32 fmbm_opso;		/* O/H Parsing Start Offset */
+	u32 fmbm_opp;		/* O/H Policer Profile */
+	u32 fmbm_occb;		/* O/H Custom (Coarse) Classification Base */
+	u32 fmbm_oim;		/* O/H Internal Margins */
+	u32 fmbm_ofp;		/* O/H FIFO Parameters */
+	u32 fmbm_ofed;		/* O/H Frame End Data */
+	u32 reserved0038[0x2];	/* (0x038-0x03F) */
+	u32 fmbm_opri[PORT_PRS_RESULT_WORDS_NUM];
+	/* O/H Parse Result Initialization */
+	u32 fmbm_ofqid;		/* O/H Frame Queue ID */
+	u32 fmbm_oefqid;	/* O/H Error Frame Queue ID */
+	u32 fmbm_ofsdm;		/* O/H Frame Status Discard Mask */
+	u32 fmbm_ofsem;		/* O/H Frame Status Error Mask */
+	u32 fmbm_ofene;		/* O/H Frame Enqueue Next Engine */
+	u32 fmbm_orlmts;	/* O/H Rate Limiter Scale */
+	u32 fmbm_orlmt;		/* O/H Rate Limiter */
+	u32 fmbm_ocmne;		/* O/H Continuous Mode Next Engine */
+	u32 reserved0080[0x38]; /* (0x080-0x15F) */
+	u32 fmbm_ocgm[PORT_CG_MAP_NUM];	/* Observed Congestion Grp Map */
+	u32 reserved0180[0x20]; /* (0x180-0x1FF) */
+	u32 fmbm_ostc;		/* O/H Statistics Counters */
+	u32 fmbm_ofrc;		/* O/H Frame Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofdc;		/* O/H Frames Discard Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofledc;	/* O/H Frames Length Error Discard Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofufdc;	/* O/H Frames Unsupported Format Discard Cntr */
+	u32 fmbm_offc;		/* O/H Filter Frames Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofwdc;		/* O/H Frames WRED Discard Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofldec;	/* O/H Frames List DMA Error Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_obdc;		/* O/H Buffers Deallocate Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_oodc;		/* O/H Out of Buffers Discard Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_opec;		/* O/H Prepare to Enqueue Counter */
+	u32 reserved022c[0x15]; /* (0x22C-0x27F) */
+	u32 fmbm_opc;		/* O/H Performance Counters */
+	u32 fmbm_opcp;		/* O/H Performance Count Parameters */
+	u32 fmbm_occn;		/* O/H Cycle Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_otuc;		/* O/H Tasks Utilization Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_oduc;		/* O/H DMA Utilization Counter */
+	u32 fmbm_ofuc;		/* O/H FIFO Utilization Counter */
+	u32 reserved0298[0x1a]; /* (0x298-0x2FF) */
+	u32 fmbm_odcfg[0x3];	/* O/H Debug Configuration */
+	u32 fmbm_ogpr;		/* O/H General Purpose Register */
+	u32 reserved0310[0x3c]; /* (0x310-0x3FF) */
+};
+
 /* BMI port register map */
 union fman_port_bmi_regs {
 	struct fman_port_rx_bmi_regs rx;
 	struct fman_port_tx_bmi_regs tx;
+	struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs oh;
 };

 /* QMI port register map */
@@ -1563,6 +1624,32 @@ struct fman_port *fman_port_lookup_rx(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_lookup_rx);

+/*
+ * fman_port_lookup_oh() -- mirrors fman_port_lookup_rx() (0115) for O/H
+ * ports. ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1): lets a later bring-up path
+ * resolve the live struct fman_port for (fman, hw O/H port id) once
+ * fman_port_probe() has registered it -- the same active-port registry, no
+ * new bookkeeping. Returns NULL if the port never probed successfully
+ * (e.g. fman_get_qman_channel_id() found no channel for that hw id) or
+ * hasn't reached fman_port_init() yet.
+ */
+struct fman_port *fman_port_lookup_oh(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id)
+{
+	struct fman_port *p, *found = NULL;
+
+	mutex_lock(&fman_port_active_lock);
+	list_for_each_entry(p, &fman_port_active_list, node) {
+		if (p->fm == fm && p->port_id == port_id &&
+		    p->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH) {
+			found = p;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&fman_port_active_lock);
+	return found;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_lookup_oh);
+
 /*
  * fman_port_set_silicon_hit_release_all -- TX bypass on all TX ports
  *
@@ -2216,6 +2303,20 @@ static int fman_port_probe(struct platform_device *of_dev)
 			port_speed = 1000;
 		port_type = FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX;

+	} else if (of_device_is_compatible(port_node, "fsl,fman-v3-port-oh")) {
+		/*
+		 * O/H port: no MAC, no link speed (RM 5.3.1). ASK2 OH-port
+		 * re-enqueue infra (dpaa1) -- probe only creates the
+		 * fman_port object and maps its BMI/QMI/HWP register window;
+		 * no register is written here (see fman_port_probe() below,
+		 * unchanged for this branch). The FMBM_OCFG[EN] bring-up
+		 * sequence (RM 5.5.7.6, 13 steps) is a separate, later
+		 * increment -- this port stays completely inert until that
+		 * lands and is explicitly armed.
+		 */
+		port_type = FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH;
+		port_speed = 0;
+
 	}  else {
 		dev_err(port->dev, "%s: Illegal port type\n", __func__);
 		err = -EINVAL;
@@ -2225,7 +2326,7 @@ static int fman_port_probe(struct platform_device *of_dev)
 	port->dts_params.type = port_type;
 	port->dts_params.speed = port_speed;

-	if (port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX) {
+	if (port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX || port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH) {
 		u32 qman_channel_id;

 		qman_channel_id = fman_get_qman_channel_id(fman, port_id);
@@ -2282,6 +2383,14 @@ static const struct of_device_id fman_port_match[] = {
 	{.compatible = "fsl,fman-v2-port-rx"},
 	{.compatible = "fsl,fman-v3-port-tx"},
 	{.compatible = "fsl,fman-v2-port-tx"},
+	/*
+	 * ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1): mainline never bound O/H
+	 * ports (confirmed live 2026-09-01 -- all 6 O/H nodes on this board,
+	 * hw id 0x02-0x07, had no driver attached). This makes them probe
+	 * and register a struct fman_port (inert -- see fman_port_probe()),
+	 * nothing more.
+	 */
+	{.compatible = "fsl,fman-v3-port-oh"},
 	{}
 };

